; Requirement: "undetermined" is a verdict: neither an identity nor a
; difference has been judged.
;
; That is a statement about what is absent, so it needs negation.
;
; Observed: a rule cannot test that a row is absent. `not` is the boolean
; operator only. cases/three-crosses/audit.egg gets "undetermined" another
; way: a boolean with :merge (or old new), read in a later ruleset.

(relation record (String))
(relation state-known (String))
(record "met/41.1.31")
(record "met/41.1.32")
(state-known "met/41.1.31")

(relation state-unknown (String))
(rule ((record r) (not (state-known r)))
      ((state-unknown r)))
(run 1)
(print-function state-unknown 10)
